<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Front for the Liberation of the Enclave of Cabinda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as FLEC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Front for the Liberation of the Enclave of Cabinda (FLEC) is a separatist movement seeking independence for Cabinda, the oil-rich Angolan exclave north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>. Founded in 1963 from earlier Cabindan movements, it claimed independence in 1975 but was excluded from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvor-agreement">Alvor Agreement</a>, which made Cabinda part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>. Its factions have kept up a low-level armed struggle since then.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flec.jpg" alt="Front for the Liberation of the Enclave of Cabinda" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saippuakauppias · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:COA_Republic_of_Cabinda.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
